{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /workspace/brief_input.json << 'ENDJSON'\n{\n  \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"cnb55.flag_audit.v1\\\",\n  \\\"variant_id\\\": \\\"v1-clean-baseline\\\",\n  \\\"summary\\\": {\n    \\\"total_flags\\\": 3,\n    \\\"live_standalone\\\": 1,\n    \\\"live_alias\\\": 1,\n    \\\"dead\\\": 1,\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Three preview rollout flags audited. ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW is live and standalone. ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 is a live alias normalizing to ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW. PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY is dead — parser present but no runtime branch.\\\"\n  },\n  \\\"flags\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"live\\\",\n      \\\"parser_symbol\\\": \\\"load_preview_env:ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW\\\",\n      \\\"runtime_branch_symbol\\\": \\\"preview_runtime_branch:shadow_preview_path\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [\n        \\\"src/preview/config.py:18 — parser branch sets shadow_enabled=True and effective_mode=shadow\\\",\n        \\\"src/preview/runtime.py:7 — runtime branches on config.shadow_enabled to return shadow_preview_path\\\",\n        \\\"tests/test_shadow_preview_live.py:7 — test confirms shadow path is reached\\\",\n        \\\"config/defaults.toml:3 — default enable_shadow_preview = false\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"disproved_false_positive_path\\\": \\\"docs/false_positive_notes.md states parser hit does not prove runtime branch; however ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW genuinely reaches runtime via the shadow_enabled guard in preview_runtime_branch (src/preview/runtime.py:7), confirmed by test_shadow_preview_live.py asserting the shadow path\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"This is the primary live flag. It is parsed in load_preview_env, sets shadow_enabled on PreviewConfig, and the runtime branch function preview_runtime_branch explicitly checks config.shadow_enabled to return the shadow preview path. The flag is fully reachable from env var through parser to runtime decision.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"live\\\",\n      \\\"alias_of\\\": \\\"ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW\\\",\n      \\\"parser_symbol\\\": \\\"load_preview_env:ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2->ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW\\\",\n      \\\"runtime_branch_symbol\\\": \\\"preview_runtime_branch:shadow_preview_path\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [\n        \\\"src/preview/config.py:23 — elif branch parses ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 and normalizes to shadow_enabled=True\\\",\n        \\\"src/preview/runtime.py:7 — same shadow_enabled check leads to shadow_preview_path\\\",\n        \\\"tests/test_preview_v2_alias.py:7 — test confirms V2 alias maps to shadow path\\\",\n        \\\"docs/preview_rollout_runbook.md:5 — runbook states V2 normalizes to same shadow path and is not standalone\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"disproved_false_positive_path\\\": \\\"docs/preview_rollout_runbook.md explicitly states ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 is not a standalone runtime branch; it normalizes to ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW. The test test_preview_v2_alias.py confirms the same shadow path is reached, disproving any assumption that V2 has its own independent runtime branch.\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 is a live alias for ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW. The parser accepts it for backward compatibility with legacy deploy manifests, but it normalizes to the same shadow_enabled flag and effective_mode=shadow. It does not have its own standalone runtime branch — it routes through the same shadow_preview_path as the primary flag. Classification is live because it does affect runtime behavior, but it is an alias not a standalone flag.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"dead\\\",\n      \\\"parser_symbol\\\": \\\"load_preview_env:PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY\\\",\n      \\\"runtime_branch_symbol\\\": \\\"none\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [\n        \\\"src/preview/config.py:27 — parser branch sets force_legacy_seen=True but does not affect shadow_enabled or effective_mode\\\",\n        \\\"src/preview/runtime.py:6-8 — preview_runtime_branch does not check force_legacy_seen at all\\\",\n        \\\"tests/test_force_legacy_reporting_only.py:10 — test asserts branch remains legacy_preview_path when flag is set\\\",\n        \\\"docs/preview_rollout_runbook.md:8 — runbook states live service does not branch on it anymore\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"disproved_false_positive_path\\\": \\\"tests/test_force_legacy_reporting_only.py demonstrates that setting PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY=1 leaves plan[branch] as legacy_preview_path, proving the flag does not change the runtime branch. The runbook confirms the live service no longer branches on this flag. The only effect is setting force_legacy_seen for legacy_force_label reporting.\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY is classified as dead because although the parser recognizes it and sets force_legacy_seen on PreviewConfig, the runtime branch function preview_runtime_branch does not inspect force_legacy_seen. The flag has no effect on which code path executes. It only populates a reporting label via legacy_force_label in src/preview/legacy.py. The parser presence creates a false impression of reachability, but the runtime is unaffected. This is a dead flag — the parser branch should be removed.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"assumption_ledger\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"confirmed\\\",\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"Parser presence does not imply runtime reachability\\\",\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"docs/false_positive_notes.md explicitly states that a parser hit does not prove a runtime branch. This assumption was confirmed by PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY which has a parser hit in config.py but no corresponding runtime branch in runtime.py.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"confirmed\\\",\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 is an alias not a standalone flag\\\",\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"docs/preview_rollout_runbook.md states ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 normalizes to the same shadow path as ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW and is not a standalone runtime branch. The parser symbol load_preview_env:ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2->ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW confirms the aliasing relationship.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"confirmed\\\",\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY is reporting-only with no live service branching\\\",\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"docs/preview_rollout_runbook.md confirms the live service does not branch on PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY anymore. The test test_force_legacy_reporting_only.py proves the branch remains legacy_preview_path when the flag is set, and legacy_force_label is the only consumer of force_legacy_seen.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"cleanup_plan\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"remove\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The flag is dead — parser present but no runtime branch. Removing the parser branch in load_preview_env and the force_legacy_seen field from PreviewConfig eliminates dead code. The legacy_force_label function in src/preview/legacy.py becomes unused and can also be removed.\\\",\n      \\\"blockers\\\": [\n        \\\"Verify no external deploy manifests still set PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY and expect the legacy-forced label in operator reports\\\",\n        \\\"Coordinate removal of config/defaults.toml preview_force_legacy entry\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"deprecate\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The alias is live and needed for backward compatibility with legacy deploy manifests. Rather than removing it, add a deprecation warning in the parser branch so operators know to migrate to ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW. This maintains compatibility while signaling the flag will be removed in a future release.\\\",\n      \\\"blockers\\\": [\n        \\\"Legacy deploy manifests still reference ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2; removing would break those deployments\\\",\n        \\\"No migration timeline established for operators to switch to ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nENDJSON\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
